CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^\[handler\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ handler only on these paths: SUCCESS$
^\[handler\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ terminate: exception leaves main: FAILURE$
^\[handler\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ terminate: exception leaves noexcept: FAILURE$
^\[handler\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ terminate: called directly: FAILURE$
^\[handler\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ handler installed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ throw\(\) is non-throwing: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 4 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
std::set_terminate, std::get_terminate and std::terminate had no body,
an exception leaving main or a noexcept function ended the program
silently, and every noexcept(...) was taken as noexcept(true).  Assertions
2 to 4 fail on one path each (handler on paths 1 to 3, and nowhere else).
